<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Dialogue Conference (Yemen)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2013">2013</a>–<a href="/years/2014">2014</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Dialogue Conference was a forum of 565 delegates held in Sanaa from March 2013 to January 2014 as part of the transition agreed after the 2011 uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. It brought together parties, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/houthi-movement">Houthis</a>, southern groups, women and youth to draft principles for a new constitution, proposing a federal state. Disputes over the federal regions contributed to the collapse of the transition in 2014.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A <b>National Dialogue Conference</b> in 2013–2014 proposed a federal state, but the transition faltered.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Republic of Yemen · Into the Present</a></li></ul></section>
